1
00:00:48,862 --> 00:00:49,696
What?

2
00:00:51,823 --> 00:00:52,782
We…

3
00:00:53,283 --> 00:00:54,993
Why are we here?

4
00:00:55,702 --> 00:00:58,079
We evacuated here
because of the typhoon, right?

5
00:00:58,163 --> 00:01:01,291
But who brought us all the way here?

6
00:01:01,374 --> 00:01:02,500
What is this place?

7
00:01:03,001 --> 00:01:04,794
-Where are we?
-Huh? What?

8
00:01:09,299 --> 00:01:10,592
It's a shrine!

9
00:01:10,675 --> 00:01:11,759
-A shrine?
-What?

10
00:01:11,843 --> 00:01:13,261
Thank you for having us.

11
00:01:18,224 --> 00:01:19,142
Huh?

12
00:01:19,851 --> 00:01:22,103
Whoa! Look at this!

13
00:01:22,187 --> 00:01:23,354
What?

14
00:01:25,815 --> 00:01:28,860
A large-scale landslide
has occurred in Tatsumi Town.

15
00:01:28,943 --> 00:01:32,739
Many local houses
were caught up in the landslide,

16
00:01:32,822 --> 00:01:34,824
but there have been no casualties.

17
00:01:36,409 --> 00:01:38,995
-Is this where the villa was?
-Yeah.

18
00:01:39,078 --> 00:01:40,830
The villa is gone!

19
00:01:40,914 --> 00:01:44,459
The road is over there,
so the villa was completely washed away!

20
00:01:45,460 --> 00:01:47,629
-This is the orange garden!
-You're right!

21
00:01:48,213 --> 00:01:49,088
Wait a minute.

22
00:01:49,172 --> 00:01:51,507
If we had stayed there,
we would have died.

23
00:01:51,591 --> 00:01:54,969
Yeah. If we hadn't left the villa
back then, by now, we would be…

24
00:01:55,053 --> 00:01:56,137
Hey!

25
00:01:56,221 --> 00:01:57,722
My grandma's ashes!

26
00:01:57,805 --> 00:02:02,310
-Grandma, the villa is gone!
-Grandma…

27
00:02:02,393 --> 00:02:03,311
They brought her…

28
00:02:03,394 --> 00:02:07,315
Is God telling us
that our vacation is over?

29
00:02:07,398 --> 00:02:08,566
God?

30
00:02:08,650 --> 00:02:11,736
What kind of god
would cause a disaster like this?

31
00:02:11,819 --> 00:02:12,695
True.

32
00:02:12,779 --> 00:02:16,074
Yeah, no god or Buddha
would do something like this!

33
00:02:20,161 --> 00:02:21,788
What kind of god helped us…

34
00:02:22,705 --> 00:02:24,999
Everyone, let's calm down!

35
00:02:25,083 --> 00:02:29,712
Come on. It's a shame that the villa
is gone, but we all survived!

36
00:02:30,338 --> 00:02:33,216
The land remains.
I will make it big as an actor…

37
00:02:33,299 --> 00:02:36,344
I'll rebuild
a Konta villa there in no time!

38
00:02:36,427 --> 00:02:38,471
Then we can all have a barbecue again!

39
00:02:38,554 --> 00:02:40,640
-Konta!
-Oh, Rinrin!

40
00:02:40,723 --> 00:02:41,683
Oh, sorry, Rinrin!

41
00:02:55,321 --> 00:02:57,281
TWO DAYS LATER

42
00:02:59,158 --> 00:03:02,328
Well, our vacation was forced to an end.

43
00:03:02,412 --> 00:03:03,705
Shall we get to work?

44
00:03:04,372 --> 00:03:06,165
No other choice…

45
00:03:07,041 --> 00:03:09,585
Everyone has to work after all.

46
00:03:10,586 --> 00:03:12,463
You can't survive without money.

47
00:03:12,547 --> 00:03:14,757
My savings ran out,
so I'll get a part-time job.

48
00:03:15,633 --> 00:03:18,344
I should also register
at a new temp agency.

49
00:03:18,928 --> 00:03:21,556
I need to find a new job.

50
00:03:21,639 --> 00:03:23,599
I will work too.

51
00:03:24,308 --> 00:03:27,311
Well, our long summer vacation is over.

52
00:03:27,395 --> 00:03:29,147
Do your best with the movie.

53
00:03:29,230 --> 00:03:31,024
Yeah, leave it to me.

54
00:03:31,107 --> 00:03:32,233
I'll do my best.

55
00:03:32,734 --> 00:03:33,651
Come on, everyone!

56
00:03:33,735 --> 00:03:36,988
-What?
-Back to society! Let's go!

57
00:03:37,071 --> 00:03:40,158
Be quiet! You're bothering
the other customers.

58
00:03:40,241 --> 00:03:42,243
-I'm sorry.
-Cut it out!

59
00:03:45,163 --> 00:03:47,081
Tetsuro. Stop paying with cash.

60
00:03:47,165 --> 00:03:49,375
-Here, use this to pay.
-Got it.

61
00:03:49,459 --> 00:03:50,293
See you all!

62
00:03:50,376 --> 00:03:52,128
-See you.
-I'll send you the money!

63
00:03:52,211 --> 00:03:53,629
-Okay.
-Bye, Midori. See you later!

64
00:03:53,713 --> 00:03:55,757
-See you!
-I'll be in touch, Konta.

65
00:03:57,133 --> 00:03:58,343
Please!

66
00:04:01,888 --> 00:04:03,056
She's too cute.

67
00:04:04,265 --> 00:04:05,350
Excuse me!

68
00:04:11,814 --> 00:04:13,608
Dad? Hello, what's wrong?

69
00:04:15,568 --> 00:04:16,944
Disaster insurance?

70
00:04:17,487 --> 00:04:18,696
Oh, right.

71
00:04:18,780 --> 00:04:21,240
You're going to the government office
to do the paperwork?

72
00:04:21,949 --> 00:04:22,784
I see.

73
00:04:22,867 --> 00:04:23,951
Okay, thank you.

74
00:04:24,577 --> 00:04:27,663
For now,
I'll take Grandma's urn to my place.

75
00:04:27,747 --> 00:04:28,581
Yeah.

76
00:04:28,664 --> 00:04:29,499
Okay.

77
00:04:29,582 --> 00:04:31,000
Dad, I'm here too!

78
00:04:31,084 --> 00:04:32,377
Sorry, I hung up.

79
00:04:32,460 --> 00:04:33,544
Never mind.

80
00:04:35,254 --> 00:04:36,756
Oh, it's my manager.

81
00:04:38,674 --> 00:04:39,842
Hello?

82
00:04:39,926 --> 00:04:40,968
Yes, I've been well.

83
00:04:41,594 --> 00:04:44,263
Oh, yes. I'm in Tokyo right now.

84
00:04:45,181 --> 00:04:46,682
Huh? Seriously?

85
00:04:47,850 --> 00:04:49,185
Yes, I'll be there.

86
00:04:49,268 --> 00:04:51,687
I'll head over right now. Yes, okay.

87
00:04:51,771 --> 00:04:52,772
I understand.

88
00:04:52,855 --> 00:04:55,233
I'll do my best. Excuse me.

89
00:04:56,526 --> 00:04:57,485
-Oh, man.
-Huh?

90
00:04:57,568 --> 00:05:00,113
I got a role. A late-night drama.
And I have lines!

91
00:05:00,196 --> 00:05:02,198
Oh, that's great!

92
00:05:02,281 --> 00:05:04,826
As I thought, Tokyo was waiting for me.

93
00:05:05,326 --> 00:05:07,537
Well, I'm off. They're already shooting.

94
00:05:07,620 --> 00:05:09,163
-Take care.
-All right. Um…

95
00:05:09,247 --> 00:05:11,791
As for the money, Midori, you pay.

96
00:05:13,668 --> 00:05:15,837
Thank you!

97
00:05:31,227 --> 00:05:32,854
Why is this spot empty?

98
00:05:49,829 --> 00:05:52,206
I need to move forward too.

99
00:05:59,213 --> 00:06:00,840
Thank you very much.

100
00:06:02,967 --> 00:06:05,178
ORANGE PEELS 500 YEN

101
00:06:11,934 --> 00:06:12,894
These too, please.

102
00:06:12,977 --> 00:06:14,520
Certainly.

103
00:06:20,234 --> 00:06:22,486
You've done something terrible.

104
00:06:25,573 --> 00:06:27,116
I'm sorry.

105
00:06:28,910 --> 00:06:31,370
I erased those humans' memories.

106
00:06:31,454 --> 00:06:34,040
No one remembers you anymore.

107
00:06:34,957 --> 00:06:40,504
Your human form has become grains of sand,
turned into sea foam,

108
00:06:40,588 --> 00:06:42,006
and vanished.

109
00:06:45,092 --> 00:06:46,052
However!

110
00:06:46,677 --> 00:06:47,595
However!

111
00:06:50,056 --> 00:06:51,724
The Dragon God

112
00:06:53,351 --> 00:06:54,810
has headhunted you.

113
00:06:55,686 --> 00:06:56,646
What?

114
00:06:57,396 --> 00:06:59,273
Japan is a land of gods.

115
00:06:59,357 --> 00:07:03,277
And the shrines that have existed there
since ancient times

116
00:07:03,861 --> 00:07:07,782
operate on different values
compared to us.

117
00:07:11,327 --> 00:07:15,164
My reason for existing
was to witness the demise of humans.

118
00:07:15,248 --> 00:07:18,167
To see them delivered to the underworld.

119
00:07:18,251 --> 00:07:19,335
But…

120
00:07:24,924 --> 00:07:27,927
I lost sight of my duties as Grim Reaper.

121
00:07:29,136 --> 00:07:31,597
And ended up saving their lives.

122
00:07:33,266 --> 00:07:34,767
Why did it come to this?

123
00:07:35,768 --> 00:07:38,396
It was an unprecedented act of misconduct.

124
00:07:39,105 --> 00:07:43,067
Why did you have to cause such trouble?

125
00:07:43,150 --> 00:07:45,236
I want to know the reason.

126
00:07:47,446 --> 00:07:48,781
Why?

127
00:07:56,872 --> 00:07:59,000
Because I was on vacation.

128
00:08:06,382 --> 00:08:10,177
I've often been told that vacations
change a person's way of thinking.

129
00:08:10,970 --> 00:08:13,764
But to think it would
even affect a Grim Reaper…

130
00:08:14,515 --> 00:08:15,349
Well…

131
00:08:16,225 --> 00:08:18,269
As a result, for better or worse,

132
00:08:18,352 --> 00:08:22,064
that god, the Dragon, has recruited you.

133
00:08:28,904 --> 00:08:32,033
Those gods over there, unlike us,

134
00:08:32,116 --> 00:08:35,161
have been helping humans
since ancient times.

135
00:08:35,244 --> 00:08:37,163
It's like their main job.

136
00:08:37,913 --> 00:08:42,209
Even a soft-hearted, good-for-nothing
Grim Reaper like you

137
00:08:42,293 --> 00:08:46,172
might have some potential,
from their point of view.

138
00:08:46,964 --> 00:08:48,341
You are the man they need…

139
00:08:48,924 --> 00:08:49,759
No,

140
00:08:50,593 --> 00:08:52,678
the god they need.

141
00:08:53,471 --> 00:08:54,722
Something like that.

142
00:08:58,184 --> 00:08:59,977
So…

143
00:09:00,061 --> 00:09:02,938
If I become a god of a shrine,

144
00:09:03,022 --> 00:09:06,484
are you going to revive me again?

145
00:09:08,152 --> 00:09:09,987
Don't get ahead of yourself.

146
00:09:10,071 --> 00:09:12,573
You won't become a god right away.

147
00:09:13,574 --> 00:09:16,160
First, you must do decades
of community service.

148
00:09:16,243 --> 00:09:19,914
No, in this case, earthly service.

149
00:09:21,457 --> 00:09:25,461
You will reflect on your transgression,
while working in their world.

150
00:09:49,402 --> 00:09:50,820
You only get one shot.

151
00:09:51,487 --> 00:09:53,114
There are no redos.

152
00:09:53,906 --> 00:09:56,325
If you hit the sea, that's where you go.

153
00:10:13,342 --> 00:10:14,719
Nice throw.

154
00:10:15,386 --> 00:10:17,263
Some fine control right there.

155
00:10:38,659 --> 00:10:39,827
-Midori.
-Yes?

156
00:10:39,910 --> 00:10:41,203
Do you want some coffee?

157
00:10:41,287 --> 00:10:42,955
Oh, not right now.

158
00:10:43,038 --> 00:10:43,998
Okay.

159
00:11:03,184 --> 00:11:04,810
Hello, Konta?

160
00:11:05,311 --> 00:11:06,812
How is the shoot going?

161
00:11:06,896 --> 00:11:09,190
Period dramas must be tough, huh?

162
00:11:09,273 --> 00:11:12,985
It's about the Great Tenpo famine,

163
00:11:13,068 --> 00:11:15,237
so it seems I have to lose weight.

164
00:11:15,321 --> 00:11:18,073
The director banned me from having lunch.

165
00:11:18,157 --> 00:11:19,074
So…

166
00:11:19,158 --> 00:11:20,409
I'm eating leaves for real!

167
00:11:23,162 --> 00:11:24,497
In order to survive…

168
00:11:25,414 --> 00:11:28,667
you even have to eat grass!

169
00:11:39,595 --> 00:11:40,763
THE GREAT TENPO FAMINE

170
00:11:40,846 --> 00:11:42,848
SHOOTING IS GOING SMOOTHLY!

171
00:11:42,932 --> 00:11:48,103
Also, Rinrin is like,
incredibly busy with work.

172
00:11:48,187 --> 00:11:50,189
We can't really meet up.

173
00:11:50,272 --> 00:11:51,357
I see.

174
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:54,443
Both of you are working so hard,
it's admirable.

175
00:11:54,527 --> 00:11:55,361
Admirable?

176
00:11:56,612 --> 00:11:57,988
Wait, what about you, Midori?

177
00:11:58,072 --> 00:11:59,406
What have you been up to?

178
00:12:00,241 --> 00:12:01,325
Me?

179
00:12:02,159 --> 00:12:03,369
Well, I…

180
00:12:09,875 --> 00:12:13,087
There you go.

181
00:12:13,170 --> 00:12:14,964
Summer oranges!

182
00:12:20,511 --> 00:12:21,804
Konta.

183
00:12:21,887 --> 00:12:23,973
Konta, do your best!

184
00:12:24,056 --> 00:12:26,600
Until you make it big, I will work too!

185
00:12:26,684 --> 00:12:31,146
In order to rebuild that villa,
you must become famous!

186
00:12:31,730 --> 00:12:32,606
Yeah!

187
00:12:33,315 --> 00:12:35,526
Rinrin, I'll do my best.

188
00:12:36,151 --> 00:12:39,113
For your sake, and to rebuild that villa,

189
00:12:39,738 --> 00:12:41,865
I'll risk my life to play this role!

190
00:12:42,575 --> 00:12:45,452
Oh, sorry. Are you rolling? Sorry.

191
00:12:45,536 --> 00:12:47,204
Oh, it's not a private call.

192
00:12:47,746 --> 00:12:49,331
A utility company called.

193
00:12:49,415 --> 00:12:50,624
Sorry, I'm so sorry.

194
00:12:51,875 --> 00:12:54,503
I got scolded! I did!

195
00:12:54,587 --> 00:12:55,713
Sorry, I'm sorry.

196
00:12:59,049 --> 00:13:01,093
ONE YEAR LATER

197
00:13:20,404 --> 00:13:22,615
It has been a year
since that vacation at the villa,

198
00:13:22,698 --> 00:13:26,076
and the environment surrounding us
has changed a lot.

199
00:13:32,833 --> 00:13:36,211
My brother is finally starting to be
recognized as an actor,

200
00:13:36,295 --> 00:13:39,006
and little by little,
work has started coming in.

201
00:13:40,215 --> 00:13:43,135
The man with the slicked-back hair
in Yama-chan,

202
00:13:43,218 --> 00:13:45,721
played by Konta Hoshino, is coming in!

203
00:13:46,764 --> 00:13:49,099
Shall I slick your hair back?

204
00:13:49,683 --> 00:13:51,727
-Good morning.
-Morning.

205
00:13:51,810 --> 00:13:54,730
Rinrin is still working
at the supermarket.

206
00:13:55,522 --> 00:13:56,857
-Oh, Manager.
-Good morning.

207
00:13:56,940 --> 00:13:58,233
-Good morning.
-Do your best today.

208
00:13:58,317 --> 00:13:59,777
I will!

209
00:14:01,945 --> 00:14:05,491
Tsumugi started a part-time gig
doing tarot readings at a theme park.

210
00:14:05,574 --> 00:14:09,453
Seems she got pretty good reviews,
so she's been doing this six days a week.

211
00:14:10,037 --> 00:14:13,374
The tarot will reveal
all about your destiny!

212
00:14:14,667 --> 00:14:16,001
Here goes!

213
00:14:18,128 --> 00:14:20,214
You are not suited for business.

214
00:14:20,798 --> 00:14:21,924
Give it up.

215
00:14:22,508 --> 00:14:23,842
Seriously?

216
00:14:27,054 --> 00:14:29,848
Tetsuro rarely contacts us,

217
00:14:29,932 --> 00:14:33,143
but it seems he is working
at a campsite with a fishing pond.

218
00:14:34,979 --> 00:14:39,525
By the way, Tetsuro also came up
with the title of the essay I am writing.

219
00:14:45,030 --> 00:14:48,826
TAKING APPLICATIONS!
BIANNUAL ESSAY CONTEST

220
00:14:49,660 --> 00:14:53,163
As you can see,
I started writing an illustrated essay.

221
00:14:54,123 --> 00:14:56,166
I'm using that summer as material.

222
00:14:56,750 --> 00:15:00,963
I wanted to leave a record
of the orange recipes from that villa.

223
00:15:01,714 --> 00:15:05,259
Not as a smartphone video,
or a social media post,

224
00:15:05,342 --> 00:15:06,677
but with my own hands.

225
00:15:08,429 --> 00:15:10,639
As a kid, I drew terrible manga.

226
00:15:11,223 --> 00:15:13,517
I haven't improved much since then,

227
00:15:14,018 --> 00:15:17,855
but I feel like if I don't draw it,
I won't be able to move on.

228
00:15:32,327 --> 00:15:35,956
I wish I had taken a picture of that sea.

229
00:17:23,939 --> 00:17:25,357
A swallowtail butterfly.

230
00:18:11,862 --> 00:18:12,821
Hey!

231
00:18:19,494 --> 00:18:20,537
You dropped this.

232
00:18:21,371 --> 00:18:22,789
A large summer orange.

233
00:18:25,167 --> 00:18:27,669
You… can have it.

234
00:18:28,253 --> 00:18:29,087
What?

235
00:18:29,796 --> 00:18:32,758
Hello, Ms. Midori.

236
00:18:35,385 --> 00:18:36,386
Hey.

237
00:18:41,975 --> 00:18:45,103
Is there anywhere nice around here?

238
00:18:51,235 --> 00:18:54,571
I came here to have a vacation.

239
00:19:03,372 --> 00:19:04,790
Vacation…

240
00:19:53,797 --> 00:19:56,341
THE VACATION PRINCIPLE

241
00:19:56,425 --> 00:20:02,848
MY SUMMER ORANGE RECIPES
BY MIDORI HOSHINO

242
00:22:23,113 --> 00:22:30,120
A VACATION FOR LIFE

243
00:22:30,203 --> 00:22:31,872
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.

